(5925854, 864111, 100393, '<td valign="top">Aahh.. Dubai. It is a nice waterfall but when I''ve tried to photograph it, I''ve never found I could make it look interesting on screen.<br/> <br/>I''m not sure you''ve convinced me it is possible.</td>', 'Aahh.. Dubai. It is a nice waterfall but when I''ve tried to photograph it, I''ve never found I could make it look interesting on screen. I''m not sure you''ve convinced me it is possible.', '2010-04-01 16:20:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(5925868, 862669, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: I really like the way you haven''t taken a conventional landscape route here - the line of colour is (of course) fantastic and (of course) makes the image. The brilliance is how the image plays with a sense of scale, compressing and expanding our horizons at the same time. I think your colour levels and luminosity is bang on too.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: Nothing at all. I really like it.<br/> <br/>Overall: I''m surprised at how much the introduction of a little bit of the unexpected can enhance an otherwise fairly dull image. With it, it has become something else entirely. Excellent.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: I really like the way you haven''t taken a conventional landscape route here - the line of colour is (of course) fantastic and (of course) makes the image. The brilliance is how the image plays with a sense of scale, compressing and expanding our horizons at the same time. I think your colour levels and luminosity is bang on too. Critical stuff: Nothing at all. I really like it. Overall: I''m surprised at how much the introduction of a little bit of the unexpected can enhance an otherwise fairly dull image. With it, it has become something else entirely. Excellent.', '2010-04-01 16:27:59.000000', NULL, 1),
(5925873, 862526, 100393, '<td valign="top">Common subject but uncommonly well done.</td>', 'Common subject but uncommonly well done.', '2010-04-01 16:29:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(5925882, 864248, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: Great shadows and some nice textures. It conveys a ''we all turn to dust feel''.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: The image doesn''t have much soul - it feels a little flat in terms of impact. I think the composition is a bit vanilla too. The top of the skull at the 1/3s point makes this feel a bit too by-the-numbers.<br/> <br/>Overall: To me a bit mundane; perhaps that was your intention - the matter-of-factness of death. If so, I can see your point - I just don''t think it makes for something that will hold a viewer''s interest for too long.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: Great shadows and some nice textures. It conveys a ''we all turn to dust feel''. Critical stuff: The image doesn''t have much soul - it feels a little flat in terms of impact. I think the composition is a bit vanilla too. The top of the skull at the 1/3s point makes this feel a bit too by-the-numbers. Overall: To me a bit mundane; perhaps that was your intention - the matter-of-factness of death. If so, I can see your point - I just don''t think it makes for something that will hold a viewer''s interest for too long.', '2010-04-01 16:35:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(5925888, 862004, 100393, '<td valign="top">Pretty stunning portrait - the sort of thing that would do well here and on 1x.</td>', 'Pretty stunning portrait - the sort of thing that would do well here and on 1x.', '2010-04-01 16:40:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(5925889, 864178, 29011, '<td valign="top">Awesome. Now I need to go make some! <br/>I like the rustic feel to the shot. All elements nicely placed though the cinnamon sticks in the back look a bit out place, sticking out from the brownie and OOF like that. I think it''s a nice idea to include them in the shot but perhaps in a different composition.</td>', 'Awesome. Now I need to go make some! I like the rustic feel to the shot. All elements nicely placed though the cinnamon sticks in the back look a bit out place, sticking out from the brownie and OOF like that. I think it''s a nice idea to include them in the shot but perhaps in a different composition.', '2010-04-01 16:40:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(5925890, 863892, 105171, '<td valign="top">Seems a little over-saturated - other wise an excellent shot.</td>', 'Seems a little over-saturated - other wise an excellent shot.', '2010-04-01 16:40:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(5925891, 863751, 29011, '<td valign="top">Good job with the lighting and color. The background is also nicely suited to the shot. It all works, except that I''m not a big fan of smoothing out the skin that much. But overall if the client is pleased, what can I say ;)</td>', 'Good job with the lighting and color. The background is also nicely suited to the shot. It all works, except that I''m not a big fan of smoothing out the skin that much. But overall if the client is pleased, what can I say ;)', '2010-04-01 16:41:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(5925892, 864378, 29011, '<td valign="top">Great use of getting that textured look in camera.</td>', 'Great use of getting that textured look in camera.', '2010-04-01 16:41:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(5925895, 864128, 29011, '<td valign="top">Congrats on the spot on exposure. It''s tricky with the white feathers. You kept the little subtle details. The composition works too. It''s a good shot but only wish it did not have the jagged sharpening effects. Looks as if there was some slight motion blur and you tried to compensate by oversharpening. This might look better in print though :)</td>', 'Congrats on the spot on exposure. It''s tricky with the white feathers. You kept the little subtle details. The composition works too. It''s a good shot but only wish it did not have the jagged sharpening effects. Looks as if there was some slight motion blur and you tried to compensate by oversharpening. This might look better in print though :)', '2010-04-01 16:42:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(5925897, 864132, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: I like this I really do, it seems to be perfectly composed and has a crafted feel as a consequence. I love the way the eye is led to the city in the distance and the way I wonder where you were standing when you shot it. The coloration works really well too.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: The horizon seems to tip up to the left.<br/> <br/>Overall: Great image - is just as likely to be well received by the mainstream audience as those who enjoy the more unusual perspectives.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: I like this I really do, it seems to be perfectly composed and has a crafted feel as a consequence. I love the way the eye is led to the city in the distance and the way I wonder where you were standing when you shot it. The coloration works really well too. Critical stuff: The horizon seems to tip up to the left. Overall: Great image - is just as likely to be well received by the mainstream audience as those who enjoy the more unusual perspectives.', '2010-04-01 16:43:17.000000', NULL, 1),
(5925900, 861147, 29011, '<td valign="top">I quite enjoy these sorta shots. The tones are rich and the texture of the petals really pop. Working with the shallow DOF, I also think the point of focus also works really well. Some might say it''s too centered but it doesn''t detract much if any.</td>', 'I quite enjoy these sorta shots. The tones are rich and the texture of the petals really pop. Working with the shallow DOF, I also think the point of focus also works really well. Some might say it''s too centered but it doesn''t detract much if any.', '2010-04-01 16:44:32.000000', NULL, 1),
(5925902, 864267, 29011, '<td valign="top">Wonderful capture of the soft interaction of Mom and baby. I would''ve only darkened the shadows a bit more, enough so that the background goes black. I reckon it would still fit the advanced editing rules as the background is already so dark(if it was so orginally). Hope someone corrects me if I''m wrong.</td>', 'Wonderful capture of the soft interaction of Mom and baby. I would''ve only darkened the shadows a bit more, enough so that the background goes black. I reckon it would still fit the advanced editing rules as the background is already so dark(if it was so orginally). Hope someone corrects me if I''m wrong.', '2010-04-01 16:44:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(5925903, 859502, 29011, '<td valign="top">Love the low perspective. So cool to see the giant clouds on the horizon and the beautiful colors up top. Great shot overall. An easy fave.</td>', 'Love the low perspective. So cool to see the giant clouds on the horizon and the beautiful colors up top. Great shot overall. An easy fave.', '2010-04-01 16:44:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(5925904, 864390, 29011, '<td valign="top">Very nicely composed and toned. My only nitpick is that it looks oversharpened. There are a number of techniques, one that I think would be nice here is where you resize down to twice the size of the intended websized resolution, sharpen up twice and then apply the final resize. Some people call it Adamus sharpening.</td>', 'Very nicely composed and toned. My only nitpick is that it looks oversharpened. There are a number of techniques, one that I think would be nice here is where you resize down to twice the size of the intended websized resolution, sharpen up twice and then apply the final resize. Some people call it Adamus sharpening.', '2010-04-01 16:45:09.000000', NULL, 1),
(5925906, 864268, 105171, '<td valign="top">This would have made a classic shot if tried in a slightly different angle.  Seems the focus is off a little  6.</td>', 'This would have made a classic shot if tried in a slightly different angle.  Seems the focus is off a little  6.', '2010-04-01 16:47:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(5925909, 862953, 105171, '<td valign="top">Great shot! Love it. 8.</td>', 'Great shot! Love it. 8.', '2010-04-01 16:48:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(5925910, 864246, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: Kind of a brave rendition of a Ladybug - lose the colour, make it look a little ugly, show another side.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: I''m not a fan of your conversion - I can see some residual blue lines; I''m not sure why are there but I am sure that (IMHO) they don''t work.<br/> <br/>Overall: I like your vision but I think the execution leaves a lot to be desired.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: Kind of a brave rendition of a Ladybug - lose the colour, make it look a little ugly, show another side. Critical stuff: I''m not a fan of your conversion - I can see some residual blue lines; I''m not sure why are there but I am sure that (IMHO) they don''t work. Overall: I like your vision but I think the execution leaves a lot to be desired.', '2010-04-01 16:48:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(5925917, 863308, 105171, '<td valign="top">Nice shot but the foreground is too disturbing.</td>', 'Nice shot but the foreground is too disturbing.', '2010-04-01 16:50:59.000000', NULL, 1),
(5925918, 863177, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: Unusual perspective, unusual coloration , especially the background. I like unusual.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: The eye is drawn to the eye and nose, yet neither of these are in focus - I feel there should at least be one part of the image to be in focus so as to anchor the eye before it explores the rest of the image.<br/> <br/>Overall: Nice to see a different POV but I think you would need perfect technicals to pull this off.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: Unusual perspective, unusual coloration , especially the background. I like unusual. Critical stuff: The eye is drawn to the eye and nose, yet neither of these are in focus - I feel there should at least be one part of the image to be in focus so as to anchor the eye before it explores the rest of the image. Overall: Nice to see a different POV but I think you would need perfect technicals to pull this off.', '2010-04-01 16:51:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(5925919, 863791, 100393, '<td valign="top">Great image - reminds me of my portrait of a wild bird image but I like the additional interest of the ensuing scrap here.</td>', 'Great image - reminds me of my portrait of a wild bird image but I like the additional interest of the ensuing scrap here.', '2010-04-01 16:53:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(5925922, 864276, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: This is just beautiful. the lighting, the perspective, the coloration, the composition - all very cinematic.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: Nothing at all.<br/> <br/>Overall: I hope this image gets appreciated - it is just so very, very well balanced.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: This is just beautiful. the lighting, the perspective, the coloration, the composition - all very cinematic. Critical stuff: Nothing at all. Overall: I hope this image gets appreciated - it is just so very, very well balanced.', '2010-04-01 16:55:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(5925923, 863788, 30049, '<td valign="top">Overall I''m generally not a fan of smoke swirl shots, sorry.  In this case it will interesting to see how you finish up as you''ve softened the swirls and gone with unconventional crop and border.  Best of luck to you.</td>', 'Overall I''m generally not a fan of smoke swirl shots, sorry.  In this case it will interesting to see how you finish up as you''ve softened the swirls and gone with unconventional crop and border.  Best of luck to you.', '2010-04-01 16:56:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(5925925, 859340, 30049, '<td valign="top">This seems quite dark and overly processed.</td>', 'This seems quite dark and overly processed.', '2010-04-01 16:57:32.000000', NULL, 1),
(5925926, 863844, 30049, '<td valign="top">This is a nice scene but it''s way over the top in the use of HDR/Topaz IMO.</td>', 'This is a nice scene but it''s way over the top in the use of HDR/Topaz IMO.', '2010-04-01 16:58:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(5925927, 864222, 30049, '<td valign="top">Looks like a world in turmoil after a nuclear holocaust (or a new settlement on Mars).</td>', 'Looks like a world in turmoil after a nuclear holocaust (or a new settlement on Mars).', '2010-04-01 16:59:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(5925931, 862958, 30049, '<td valign="top">A bit soft.  I do have to admit after seeing this up close I can now tell that it''s really a flower.  This object in the ''Orange'' challenge looked more like a stick with orange paper on it.</td>', 'A bit soft.  I do have to admit after seeing this up close I can now tell that it''s really a flower.  This object in the ''Orange'' challenge looked more like a stick with orange paper on it.', '2010-04-01 17:01:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(5925933, 864406, 30049, '<td valign="top">Looks like this was run through a noise reduction program several times and all detail is totally gone.</td>', 'Looks like this was run through a noise reduction program several times and all detail is totally gone.', '2010-04-01 17:02:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(5925934, 864291, 30049, '<td valign="top">A little on the bizarre side for my taste.  Nonetheless, good luck in the challenge.</td>', 'A little on the bizarre side for my taste.  Nonetheless, good luck in the challenge.', '2010-04-01 17:02:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(5925935, 863727, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: Well - I was never sure how to address the ''All things being equal'' challenge. This is inspiring! Lovely composition - the title actually really helps the eye to decode the image too. Great colours and bags of interest.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: Focus - I can''t help but think that I''d like to see the moth in sharper focus.<br/> <br/>Overall: Very unusual FS entry. Very put-on-the-wall-able too. Great stuff.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: Well - I was never sure how to address the ''All things being equal'' challenge. This is inspiring! Lovely composition - the title actually really helps the eye to decode the image too. Great colours and bags of interest. Critical stuff: Focus - I can''t help but think that I''d like to see the moth in sharper focus. Overall: Very unusual FS entry. Very put-on-the-wall-able too. Great stuff.', '2010-04-01 17:03:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(5925937, 863677, 30049, '<td valign="top">This seems to have gone from a photo to a graphic image now with the B/W conversion.  The bottom area of black makes it feel like the image is still loading and hasn''t finished.</td>', 'This seems to have gone from a photo to a graphic image now with the B/W conversion.  The bottom area of black makes it feel like the image is still loading and hasn''t finished.', '2010-04-01 17:04:17.000000', NULL, 1),
(5925939, 863932, 30049, '<td valign="top">Eyes seem over sharpened and the face is unnaturally smooth.</td>', 'Eyes seem over sharpened and the face is unnaturally smooth.', '2010-04-01 17:05:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(5925942, 864197, 30049, '<td valign="top">It''s nice, but I almost wonder if it would be even better if you''d waited a few more minutes for the sun to dip below the horizon.</td>', 'It''s nice, but I almost wonder if it would be even better if you''d waited a few more minutes for the sun to dip below the horizon.', '2010-04-01 17:07:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(5925944, 864387, 30049, '<td valign="top">Nice sunburst.  The arches are cool, but the visual beyond the arch is kinda ho-humish.  JMO of course.  Good luck.</td>', 'Nice sunburst.  The arches are cool, but the visual beyond the arch is kinda ho-humish.  JMO of course.  Good luck.', '2010-04-01 17:08:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(5925951, 864111, 30049, '<td valign="top">An interesting piece of artwork you''ve come across here.  The "back" seems not as well defined as the "calf/feet" area...maybe some selective sharpening would help (or a deeper aperture)?</td>', 'An interesting piece of artwork you''ve come across here.  The "back" seems not as well defined as the "calf/feet" area...maybe some selective sharpening would help (or a deeper aperture)?', '2010-04-01 17:10:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(5925968, 862045, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: Copenhagen Metro? This is a very well executed image - quite precise and clinical, like the Metro itself. My favourite part of the image is the reflection in the left panel.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: Other than the reflection I find the image a little sterile and the tones of the monochrome conversion do little to add drama.<br/> <br/>Overall: I do like the image but I am sure you could have got more out of the scene by playing with the reflections a little more.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: Copenhagen Metro? This is a very well executed image - quite precise and clinical, like the Metro itself. My favourite part of the image is the reflection in the left panel. Critical stuff: Other than the reflection I find the image a little sterile and the tones of the monochrome conversion do little to add drama. Overall: I do like the image but I am sure you could have got more out of the scene by playing with the reflections a little more.', '2010-04-01 17:22:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(5925973, 860965, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: Completely bizarre composition - I love that you''ve stuffed something so random into a FS. Ummm.... what else?<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: I could just say ''why'' but you would say ''why not?'' and rightly so. I am normally a fan of grain but here - this gritty, noisy look is a little ugly.<br/> <br/>Overall: I get the feeling you know exactly what you are doing here.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: Completely bizarre composition - I love that you''ve stuffed something so random into a FS. Ummm.... what else? Critical stuff: I could just say ''why'' but you would say ''why not?'' and rightly so. I am normally a fan of grain but here - this gritty, noisy look is a little ugly. Overall: I get the feeling you know exactly what you are doing here.', '2010-04-01 17:26:21.000000', NULL, 1),
