(5926345, 863392, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: Very well executed - perfect technicals, great title and a mood well conveyed. There is something about this image that is so un-snapshot; despite it having so many family snapshot elements.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: I do like it a lot - I think a monochrome conversion would work really well too.<br/> <br/>Overall: A very nice image with just the right amount of edge - I hope it does well for you.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: Very well executed - perfect technicals, great title and a mood well conveyed. There is something about this image that is so un-snapshot; despite it having so many family snapshot elements. Critical stuff: I do like it a lot - I think a monochrome conversion would work really well too. Overall: A very nice image with just the right amount of edge - I hope it does well for you.', '2010-04-01 19:59:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(5926361, 863886, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: I think fog can be quite hard to work with - I find capturing the quality of the light difficult, but you have done that here. I really like the coloration too - it hasn''t escaped me that the bottom edge is black and the top is white and how we journey through green and yellow to get there. That subtle colour change guides the eye almost without us noticing.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: Because I like the white at the top, I''m not a fan of the vignetted corners.<br/> <br/>Overall: Uber-subtle and effective.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: I think fog can be quite hard to work with - I find capturing the quality of the light difficult, but you have done that here. I really like the coloration too - it hasn''t escaped me that the bottom edge is black and the top is white and how we journey through green and yellow to get there. That subtle colour change guides the eye almost without us noticing. Critical stuff: Because I like the white at the top, I''m not a fan of the vignetted corners. Overall: Uber-subtle and effective.', '2010-04-01 20:04:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(5926374, 863785, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: You''ll be getting killed for the blur but I think it is masterful - the restriction of clarity makes us keep our distance and the paradoxically the image becomes more intimate, we feel like we are watching something authentic and uninfluenced by observation. The coloration matches the scene perfectly - I feel like I am watching a silent 8mm film, so with the (not) crashing waves - your title is perfect.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: Nothing<br/> <br/>Overall: Excellent work.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: You''ll be getting killed for the blur but I think it is masterful - the restriction of clarity makes us keep our distance and the paradoxically the image becomes more intimate, we feel like we are watching something authentic and uninfluenced by observation. The coloration matches the scene perfectly - I feel like I am watching a silent 8mm film, so with the (not) crashing waves - your title is perfect. Critical stuff: Nothing Overall: Excellent work.', '2010-04-01 20:09:42.000000', NULL, 1),
