(5937903, 864387, 47852, '<td valign="top">I thought this might be Union!  I much prefer this shot over the one you entered in the fine arts challenge... the warmth of the light and the burst around the sun are fantastic here.</td>', 'I thought this might be Union!  I much prefer this shot over the one you entered in the fine arts challenge... the warmth of the light and the burst around the sun are fantastic here.', '2010-04-08 20:15:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(5937948, 864346, 30982, '<td valign="top">As a possible explanation to Louis - this has a sense of ethereal suspension.  Somehow, Rina managed to get the animals and the wee bit of fence suspended in time, whilst all around is motion.  And suspended in a wee bit of magical light as well.  The "that doesn''t jive" feel of having part of the photo "stopped" and the rest still moving, along with the way cool light, is I think what does it for me.  But as with anytying, your mileage may vary!</td>', 'As a possible explanation to Louis - this has a sense of ethereal suspension.  Somehow, Rina managed to get the animals and the wee bit of fence suspended in time, whilst all around is motion.  And suspended in a wee bit of magical light as well.  The "that doesn''t jive" feel of having part of the photo "stopped" and the rest still moving, along with the way cool light, is I think what does it for me.  But as with anytying, your mileage may vary!', '2010-04-08 21:07:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(5937960, 863408, 76335, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by SoulJance:</b></div><hr/><i>Did you consider going in and removing all the foot prints? </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Yes. And you should have cloned out the distracting couple too. (?!)</td>', 'Originally posted by SoulJance:Did you consider going in and removing all the foot prints?   Yes. And you should have cloned out the distracting couple too. (?!)', '2010-04-08 21:23:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(5937971, 859340, 76335, '<td valign="top">I love how you composed this. Very effective.</td>', 'I love how you composed this. Very effective.', '2010-04-08 21:33:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(5937977, 859740, 76335, '<td valign="top">Well, I try to be honest -- the risk, of course, being that I might step on the toes of someone I really admire. Title and border aside, I do like this. The crop still feels a little tight to me, but there is definitely some intriguing energy between the people and whatever is on the hill. Given that -- and now that I think about it -- I can''t come up with a better title.</td>', 'Well, I try to be honest -- the risk, of course, being that I might step on the toes of someone I really admire. Title and border aside, I do like this. The crop still feels a little tight to me, but there is definitely some intriguing energy between the people and whatever is on the hill. Given that -- and now that I think about it -- I can''t come up with a better title.', '2010-04-08 21:40:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(5937979, 861323, 76335, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by bvy:</b></div><hr/><i> A fantastic composition ruined by selective desat. </i></td></tr></table> <br/>I meant to revise my comment before the challenge ended -- it was a bit harsh. I do love the composition, and I think the lines and shapes and fragmented nature of the composition were enough to hold the viewer''s interest. I''ve seen worse applications of selective desat, but I think this would have held up nicely as a straight black and white, or with a very subtle, but uniform color scheme.</td>', 'Originally posted by bvy: A fantastic composition ruined by selective desat.  I meant to revise my comment before the challenge ended -- it was a bit harsh. I do love the composition, and I think the lines and shapes and fragmented nature of the composition were enough to hold the viewer''s interest. I''ve seen worse applications of selective desat, but I think this would have held up nicely as a straight black and white, or with a very subtle, but uniform color scheme.', '2010-04-08 21:46:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(5937981, 862004, 23226, '<td valign="top">At first I thought I was looking at a piece of wood...and then I realized it was an old lady. Alright...slight exaggeration (sort of). Very nice shot.</td>', 'At first I thought I was looking at a piece of wood...and then I realized it was an old lady. Alright...slight exaggeration (sort of). Very nice shot.', '2010-04-08 21:47:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(5937984, 859045, 76335, '<td valign="top">An eight from me. I''m glad to hear that it wasn''t set up or composed -- that you photographed them as you found them. I had to give you the benefit of the doubt of course. Great shot.</td>', 'An eight from me. I''m glad to hear that it wasn''t set up or composed -- that you photographed them as you found them. I had to give you the benefit of the doubt of course. Great shot.', '2010-04-08 21:49:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(5937987, 864150, 76335, '<td valign="top">Wonderful shot. A seven from me.</td>', 'Wonderful shot. A seven from me.', '2010-04-08 21:53:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(5938011, 862976, 76335, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by scooter88:</b></div><hr/><i> Could use a little more contrast but over all nice shot. 7 </i></td></tr></table> <br/>No! The contrast was perfect. You would have risked losing too much detail if you started fussing with levels or curves. In this case, the subject, the composition alone, delivers all the impact.</td>', 'Originally posted by scooter88: Could use a little more contrast but over all nice shot. 7  No! The contrast was perfect. You would have risked losing too much detail if you started fussing with levels or curves. In this case, the subject, the composition alone, delivers all the impact.', '2010-04-08 22:11:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(5938074, 864346, 50695, '<td valign="top">To me this is Dali meets Hopper, and I love how the right side sweeps up into oblivion.</td>', 'To me this is Dali meets Hopper, and I love how the right side sweeps up into oblivion.', '2010-04-08 23:03:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(5938083, 863392, 50695, '<td valign="top">There are subtle touches that take this over the top. All the other children are in poses that suggest action (but also *re*action to the violent water spray), and all of their faces are hidden, but goggle-boy stares at us fearlessly.</td>', 'There are subtle touches that take this over the top. All the other children are in poses that suggest action (but also *re*action to the violent water spray), and all of their faces are hidden, but goggle-boy stares at us fearlessly.', '2010-04-08 23:06:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(5938091, 864365, 50695, '<td valign="top">I love the composition, so balanced and stable to contrast with the subject.</td>', 'I love the composition, so balanced and stable to contrast with the subject.', '2010-04-08 23:09:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(5938097, 864408, 50695, '<td valign="top">what''s to photoshop? you''re done.</td>', 'what''s to photoshop? you''re done.', '2010-04-08 23:12:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(5938099, 864250, 50695, '<td valign="top">The trick is two beautiful faces not quite lining up, which is creating a third, frightening face... an allegory about not fitting in and not being understood.</td>', 'The trick is two beautiful faces not quite lining up, which is creating a third, frightening face... an allegory about not fitting in and not being understood.', '2010-04-08 23:13:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(5938100, 864399, 50695, '<td valign="top">wonderful roiling delirious composition.</td>', 'wonderful roiling delirious composition.', '2010-04-08 23:14:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(5938101, 864261, 50695, '<td valign="top">I try to take pictures like this all the time and never quite make it. Well done.</td>', 'I try to take pictures like this all the time and never quite make it. Well done.', '2010-04-08 23:14:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(5938102, 863788, 50695, '<td valign="top">I *hate* smoke photos, I hate jellyfish photos and I hate baby photos, but in this challenge all 3 were transformed by the photographer, and got 10s from me.</td>', 'I *hate* smoke photos, I hate jellyfish photos and I hate baby photos, but in this challenge all 3 were transformed by the photographer, and got 10s from me.', '2010-04-08 23:18:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(5938108, 859045, 50695, '<td valign="top">9 from me ... almost a conceptual art piece.</td>', '9 from me ... almost a conceptual art piece.', '2010-04-08 23:23:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(5938117, 863132, 100831, '<td valign="top">I was in Portland last summer but when we went to Canon Beach it was raining cats and dogs!!! Even in the bad weather we got some great shots and a fabulous lunch!<br/>You did a really nice job capturing the feel of the place (silhouettes and all) with a perfect exposure.</td>', 'I was in Portland last summer but when we went to Canon Beach it was raining cats and dogs!!! Even in the bad weather we got some great shots and a fabulous lunch!You did a really nice job capturing the feel of the place (silhouettes and all) with a perfect exposure.', '2010-04-08 23:32:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(5938167, 863940, 14476, '<td valign="top"><b>Greetings from the Critique Club</b> <br/> <br/>Oh, <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=59029" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">Snaffles</a>, we meet again!  And what a fun entry you have in the Free Study.  It is easy to see why you would select it to put in the Challenge.<br/> <br/>Some of your comments noted that the sky was a bit bland, and I played with your image just a little using Shadows &amp; Highlights.  Now that''s a very useful tool for situations such as this, and I found it put a bit more light into that clever horse''s neck and deepened the blues dramatically.  Just a thought, of course.<br/> <br/>Your "V" with the fence poles and the clever boot at the right top worked quite well but could have stood a bit more color. Nevertheless, this, as <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=30982" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">Melethia</a> says, is cute and quirky and I''m glad to have seen it again.<br/> <br/></td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club  Oh,  Snaffles, we meet again!  And what a fun entry you have in the Free Study.  It is easy to see why you would select it to put in the Challenge. Some of your comments noted that the sky was a bit bland, and I played with your image just a little using Shadows & Highlights.  Now that''s a very useful tool for situations such as this, and I found it put a bit more light into that clever horse''s neck and deepened the blues dramatically.  Just a thought, of course. Your "V" with the fence poles and the clever boot at the right top worked quite well but could have stood a bit more color. Nevertheless, this, as  Melethia says, is cute and quirky and I''m glad to have seen it again. ', '2010-04-08 23:58:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(5938266, 863791, 109478, '<td valign="top">Contratulations for the top 10. <br/>How did you do for white backgound? Did you put a very big white background behind the birds or blow out the sky?</td>', 'Contratulations for the top 10. How did you do for white backgound? Did you put a very big white background behind the birds or blow out the sky?', '2010-04-09 01:45:14.000000', NULL, 0),
