(5941435, 861576, 46097, '<td valign="top">Veeeva Bafana Bafana, Viva!<br/>Absolutely amazing shot, unrivalled. So meaningful to me, on so many levels.<br/>It has technical excellence, a sense of drama, and is oh so topical, with the World Cup about to begin.<br/>One thing......if Fifa approach you, and ask to buy the rights to this photo, please get back to your DPC friends, and let us know! I would not be the least bit surprised.</td>', 'Veeeva Bafana Bafana, Viva!Absolutely amazing shot, unrivalled. So meaningful to me, on so many levels.It has technical excellence, a sense of drama, and is oh so topical, with the World Cup about to begin.One thing......if Fifa approach you, and ask to buy the rights to this photo, please get back to your DPC friends, and let us know! I would not be the least bit surprised.', '2010-04-12 05:44:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(5941451, 862526, 9668, '<td valign="top"><b>Greetings from the Critique Club! </b> <br/> <br/><b>Composition and Lighting:</b> Pretty straight forward and yet not at all. I don''t often see such high contrast images on DPC, and that isn''t a big surprise because I think they may be too artistic for DPC - kind of like this image. Anyways, I love the creativity of this image. Lovely contrasts. <br/>Thou what is with the trend of black borders on the top and bottom? <br/> <br/><b>Technical:</b> Larger! I agree. Why constrain yourself to 616 pixels wide? Also, nitpicking, it bothers me that some lashes are totally blurry and others seem overly sharp. <br/> <br/><b>Overall:</b> I do like it! First shot of an eye, awesome job. Keep up the good work. <br/></td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club!   Composition and Lighting: Pretty straight forward and yet not at all. I don''t often see such high contrast images on DPC, and that isn''t a big surprise because I think they may be too artistic for DPC - kind of like this image. Anyways, I love the creativity of this image. Lovely contrasts. Thou what is with the trend of black borders on the top and bottom?  Technical: Larger! I agree. Why constrain yourself to 616 pixels wide? Also, nitpicking, it bothers me that some lashes are totally blurry and others seem overly sharp.  Overall: I do like it! First shot of an eye, awesome job. Keep up the good work. ', '2010-04-12 06:01:54.000000', NULL, 0),
