(5943269, 864184, 95418, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club.<br/> <br/>Great picture, congrats ( Lava falls )!<br/> <br/>Some ideas you may like:<br/> <br/>1 = Add more contrast. This could give more life to your photo!<br/>2 = Next time you can get the picture a little bit away from the suject. I believe that the picture will be more easy to undestand/decode.<br/>3 = Insert a border and your signature there!<br/> <br/>Hope you like the ideas!<br/> <br/>Tell me what you think about my ideas.<br/> <br/>Regards,<br/> <br/>Oscar Burd</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club. Great picture, congrats ( Lava falls )! Some ideas you may like: 1 = Add more contrast. This could give more life to your photo!2 = Next time you can get the picture a little bit away from the suject. I believe that the picture will be more easy to undestand/decode.3 = Insert a border and your signature there! Hope you like the ideas! Tell me what you think about my ideas. Regards, Oscar Burd', '2010-04-12 22:11:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(5943494, 861548, 106543, '<td valign="top"><b>Greetings from the Critique Club! </b> <br/> <br/>I think that the vignetting is the biggest thing hurting you here. Especially on the left it is unnaturally dark. Also I''d suggest a bigger aperture (smaller number). It would do great to have the background more out of focus with just the flowers sharp. With your lens I''d try f/4.<br/> <br/>I like the gradient from white to purple on the flower petals, the exposure is good there. Just wish the flowers had been more of a focal point.<br/> <br/>If you have any questions <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/messaging.php?action=compose&amp;USER_ID=106543" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">click here to message me</a>! <br/> <br/>Senay</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club!   I think that the vignetting is the biggest thing hurting you here. Especially on the left it is unnaturally dark. Also I''d suggest a bigger aperture (smaller number). It would do great to have the background more out of focus with just the flowers sharp. With your lens I''d try f/4. I like the gradient from white to purple on the flower petals, the exposure is good there. Just wish the flowers had been more of a focal point. If you have any questions click here to message me!  Senay', '2010-04-13 00:17:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(5943523, 863212, 106543, '<td valign="top"><b>Greetings from the Critique Club! </b> <br/> <br/>The lighting is great, however I do agree with the comment that the background is a distracting. I like the bridge part but the fence and cars, although I guess there isn''t really anything that can be done about that.<br/> <br/>You mentioned the slight blur on the helmet, but honestly it''s very minor and most people might not have noticed.<br/> <br/>Not really sure what you could do to improve this, you stopped the motion wonderfully. By looking at your votes received you can see most of the votes you got were 6 and fell off from there. You had a good picture but just not enough to get the extremely high votes.<br/> <br/>If you have any questions <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/messaging.php?action=compose&amp;USER_ID=106543" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">click here to message me</a>! <br/> <br/>Senay</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club!   The lighting is great, however I do agree with the comment that the background is a distracting. I like the bridge part but the fence and cars, although I guess there isn''t really anything that can be done about that. You mentioned the slight blur on the helmet, but honestly it''s very minor and most people might not have noticed. Not really sure what you could do to improve this, you stopped the motion wonderfully. By looking at your votes received you can see most of the votes you got were 6 and fell off from there. You had a good picture but just not enough to get the extremely high votes. If you have any questions click here to message me!  Senay', '2010-04-13 01:02:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(5943568, 862900, 106543, '<td valign="top"><b>Greetings from the Critique Club! </b> <br/> <br/>Super Dog! Very interesting photo with a lot going on. It takes more than just a glance to fully appreciate your picture. And I think that''s what might have hurt you in voting. Between the graffiti, the train, lights in the background and the flowing river (nicely captured by the way!) it''s a lot to take in with one glance.<br/> <br/>From looking at your profile it looks like these type of night shots are your specialty. Kepp up the good work!<br/> <br/>If you have any questions <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/messaging.php?action=compose&amp;USER_ID=106543" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">click here to message me</a>! <br/> <br/>Senay</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club!   Super Dog! Very interesting photo with a lot going on. It takes more than just a glance to fully appreciate your picture. And I think that''s what might have hurt you in voting. Between the graffiti, the train, lights in the background and the flowing river (nicely captured by the way!) it''s a lot to take in with one glance. From looking at your profile it looks like these type of night shots are your specialty. Kepp up the good work! If you have any questions click here to message me!  Senay', '2010-04-13 01:39:56.000000', NULL, 0),
